bital module source stages preserve physical work and unsupported tank activation]==] [==[Orbital idle modules do not invent work or storage electricity demand]==] [==[Orbital per-cell foreground bounds retain world anchors and physical approach clearance]==] [==[Orbital Assembly source follows actual native paid work and typed waits]==] [==[Orbital module rendering preserves original native owners and actor boundaries]==] [==[Industry publishes canonical asteroid class and size definitions]==] [==[Asteroid reserve sampling includes both endpoints before size scaling]==] [==[Asteroid reserves support canonical full loads and bounded mining duration]==] [==[Asteroid trajectory presentation uses bounded signed native motion without moving it]==] [==[Asteroid inspector discloses native quantities only to the surveyed company]==] [==[Bounded asteroid starter selection matches the complete grid including distance ties]==] [==[Asteroid population and placement records belong to the selected Industry profile]==] [==[World asteroid starter search uses real launch geometry and preserves feature RNG ownership]==] [==[Asteroid initial access records validate frozen bounds and explicit legacy absence]==] [==[Asteroid motion catalogue preserves the saved heading speed and feature stream]==] [==[Asteroid fractional travel is exact on every heading and speed]==] [==[Asteroid reflection translates attachment envelopes without rotating offsets]==] [==[Asteroid maximum drift fits numerical starter pursuit and travel budgets]==] [==[Depleted asteroid records retain identity resources and motion]==] [==[Asteroid removal is unsupported and invalid identities never alias depleted targets]==] [==[Static module footprints and approaches reserve the shared outer regions]==] [==[Reflected body envelopes and attached points cannot enter static regions]==] [==[Space company indexing excludes effects and preserves all old fleet window numbers]==] [==[Small probe tuning belongs to the existing p